        "abstractEn": "A cross-sectional study of 52 transplant recipients (28 kidney and 24 liver) at Imam Reza and Montaserieh hospitals in Mashhad. Severe COVID-19 was reported in 61% of the patients. There was no significant difference between the two groups except in cough and a few laboratory tests (creatinine, ALP, total bilirubin, and PTT). All kidney recipients survived, but two patients in the liver group died, which was not statistically significant. Conclusion: mortality was higher in liver recipients.",
